      "content": "I hear you, and it does sound incredibly challenging when you see a recurring pattern in your family. It's important to acknowledge your feelings of frustration and fear for your future, and these are valid. However, biology does have room for exceptions and surprises. While genetics can increase the likelihood of certain conditions, technological advancements and lifestyle choices can sometimes alter the course. Talking to a doctor, genetic counselor, or specialist might provide more personalized insight into options, potential treatments, and management strategies that could help improve your quality of life. There's value in exploring every possibility, and your unique experiences and challenges can't be fully predicted by past patterns. Sometimes, belief in hope and seeking support can be powerful steps for its own sake, even if it feels uncertain. You're not bound by the cycle; you have the power to shape your destiny, even within constraints.",
